# Limitless — Complete Frontend Integration & Workflow Guide

This document maps the complete end-to-end user workflows for the **Limitless** Cognitive Performance platform. It provides the frontend developer with exact API endpoints, request/response payloads, and base URLs required to build and verify the client application.

---

## 1. Architecture & Service Base URLs

The application communicates with two distinct backend services. All requests must use the base URLs listed below:

| Service | Production Base URL | Purpose / Responsibilities |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Node.js Backend** | `https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io` | User authentication, OTP verification, user profile management, saving assessments, storing and serving PDF reports, and contact enquiries. |
| **Python AI Model Service** | `https://limitless-model.160-153-179-249.sslip.io` | Running AI models for generating dynamic assessment questions, analyzing cognitive responses, and performing longitudinal/trend analysis across multiple assessments. |

> [!WARNING]
> **CORS & Proxying Rule:**
> To prevent CORS issues, do NOT call the Python AI Model Service URL directly from the client browser. 
> - **AI endpoints** must be called using the `getApiUrl()` helper from `src/lib/apiUtils.js` which routes requests through a same-origin proxy (Vite proxy in local development, Nginx `/api/` on production, or `api-proxy.php` on PHP hosting).
> - **Node.js Backend endpoints** are CORS-enabled and can be called directly using the helpers in `src/lib/backendApi.js`.

---

## 2. Global State & Storage Contracts

The frontend manages user sessions using `sessionStorage`. Below is the list of expected keys:

| `sessionStorage` Key | Type | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `authToken` | String | JWT token returned upon user register or login. Include in headers: `Authorization: Bearer <authToken>`. |
| `isLoggedIn` | Boolean | `true` if the user is authenticated. |
| `userId` | String | The database identifier of the currently logged-in user. |
| `userEmail` | String | Registered email address of the user. |
| `name` | String | Full name of the user. |
| `userAge` | Integer | User age. Used in question generation. |
| `userGender` | String | User gender. Used in question generation. |
| `paymentStatus` | String | Current payment status (`"pending"`, `"paid"`, `"demo"`, `"free"`, `"trial"`, `"suspended"`). |
| `passwordResetRequired` | Boolean | Indicates if the user is using a temporary password and must reset it. |
| `assessmentId` | String | The current active assessment ID generated by the Python service. |
| `analysisReport` | JSON String | The cached result of the AI analysis. |

---

## 3. End-to-End User Workflow & API Blueprint

The diagrams and sections below describe the step-by-step journey of a user interacting with the platform.

### Workflow Overview

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User Browser
    participant FE as Frontend App
    participant Node as Node.js Backend<br/>(port 4000)
    participant AI as Python AI Service<br/>(port 8001)

    Note over User, AI: Step 1: Pre-Registration & Verification
    User->>FE: Enters Email & Name
    FE->>Node: POST /api/auth/send-otp
    Node-->>User: Sends 6-Digit Code via Email
    User->>FE: Enters 6-Digit Code
    FE->>Node: POST /api/auth/verify-otp
    Node-->>FE: Returns { verified: true } (valid for 30m)

    Note over User, AI: Step 2: Account Creation
    User->>FE: Submits Registration Form
    FE->>Node: POST /api/auth/register
    Node-->>FE: Returns { user, tempPassword, token }
    Note over FE: Store token as "authToken"<br/>and user details in sessionStorage

    Note over User, AI: Step 3: Login & Password Reset
    User->>FE: Logs in or Resets Temp Password
    FE->>Node: POST /api/auth/change-password
    Node-->>FE: Resets password, clears reset flag

    Note over User, AI: Step 4: Dynamic Assessment
    User->>FE: Starts Assessment
    FE->>AI: POST /api/v1/generate-questions (via Proxy)
    AI-->>FE: Returns sections & custom questions
    User->>FE: Completes assessment questions
    FE->>AI: POST /api/v1/analyze (via Proxy)
    AI-->>FE: Returns report_json (scores, metrics)

    Note over User, AI: Step 5: Save & Generate Report
    FE->>Node: POST /api/assessments (Saves report_json)
    Node-->>FE: Persists assessment record
    FE->>Node: POST /api/reports/:userId/pdf (Generates & Emails PDF)
    Node->>AI: Requests PDF creation
    AI-->>Node: Returns binary PDF
    Node-->>User: Emails PDF Link & saves pdf_url
    Node-->>FE: Returns public pdfUrl
```

---

### Step-by-Step API Specification

#### Step 1: Send OTP for Verification (Public)
Before registering, the user must verify their email.
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/auth/send-otp`
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "name": "John Doe"
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "sent": true,
      "expiresInMinutes": 10
    }
    ```
    *(Note: In non-production environments where SMTP is disabled, the response will also return a `"devOtp": "XXXXXX"` key containing the generated OTP code for automated testing/debugging).*
*   **Response (Errors):**
    *   `409 Conflict`: Email already exists in the database.
    *   `429 Too Many Requests`: Resend cooldown of 60 seconds is active.

#### Step 2: Verify OTP Code (Public)
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/auth/verify-otp`
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "otp": "123456"
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "verified": true
    }
    ```
    *(Note: Once verified, the email is whitelisted to register within the next 30 minutes).*
*   **Response (Error `400`):**
    ```json
    {
      "error": "OTP invalid"
    }
    ```

#### Step 3: User Registration (Public)
Creates the account. Requires a verified email (unless `OTP_REQUIRED=false` on backend).
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/auth/register`
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "age": 28,
      "gender": "male",
      "paymentStatus": "demo", // Options: "pending" (default), "demo", "free"
      "passwordResetRequired": true
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `201`):**
    ```json
    {
      "user": {
        "id": "6a4f5b...",
        "name": "John Doe",
        "email": "user@example.com",
        "password_reset_required": true,
        "payment_status": "demo",
        "age": 28,
        "gender": "male",
        "created_at": "2026-07-27T10:18:04Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-07-27T10:18:04Z"
      },
      "tempPassword": "8CHARPWD",
      "token": "eyJhbGciOi..."
    }
    ```
    *Developer Action: Set `sessionStorage.setItem('authToken', token)` and store user credentials.*

#### Step 4: Login (Public)
Logs in using either the generated temporary password or their custom password.
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/auth/login`
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "password": "temp_or_custom_password"
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "token": "eyJhbGciOi...",
      "user": {
        "id": "6a4f5b...",
        "name": "John Doe",
        "email": "user@example.com",
        "password_reset_required": true,
        "payment_status": "demo",
        "age": 28,
        "gender": "male",
        "created_at": "2026-07-27T10:18:04Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-07-27T10:18:04Z"
      },
      "latestAssessment": null
    }
    ```

#### Step 5: Change Password / Reset Temp Password (Public/Authenticated)
Used when resetting the temporary password. Clears the `password_reset_required` flag on success.
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/auth/change-password`
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "currentPassword": "tempPassword",
      "newPassword": "newSecurePassword123"
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "message": "Password updated successfully"
    }
    ```

#### Step 6: Generate Assessment Questions (AI Model Service)
Fetches dynamic assessment questions personalized to the user's demographic traits.
*   **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/generate-questions` (Proxied to `https://limitless-model.160-153-179-249.sslip.io`)
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "age": 28,
      "gender": "male",
      "locale": "en"
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "assessmentId": "assess_99a8b...",
      "sections": [
        {
          "id": "sec_memory",
          "title": "Short Term Memory",
          "items": [
            { "id": "q1", "text": "Can you recall a list of 5 words immediately?" },
            { "id": "q2", "text": "Do you struggle to recall names of new acquaintances?" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
    ```

---

### Deep Dive: Dynamic Assessment Engine & Interactive Question Flow

This section details how questions are generated, structured, rendered on the frontend, and how responses are prepared and submitted to the API.

#### A. Generating Questions (Demographics & Triggering)
1. **Data Source:** User's age and gender are gathered from the Registration/Onboarding form (or retrieved from `sessionStorage` `/api/users/:userId` cache if the user is already authenticated).
2. **Gender Normalization:** Prior to sending to the API, genders must be normalized to prevent backend model validation failures:
   * `"male"` & `"female"` remain unchanged.
   * `"non_binary"` must be mapped to `"other"`.
   * `"prefer_not_to_say"` must be mapped to `"prefer-not-to-say"`.
3. **API Call:** The frontend sends a `POST` request to `/api/v1/generate-questions` with `age`, normalized `gender`, and `locale`.
4. **Data Flattening:** The API returns questions grouped under category sections (e.g., Short Term Memory, Focus). To render them sequentially or step-by-step, the frontend flattens the nested `items` array and injects the corresponding section title as a `domain` property:
   ```javascript
   const flatQuestions = [];
   response.sections.forEach(section => {
     (section.items || []).forEach(item => {
       flatQuestions.push({
         ...item,
         domain: section.title // E.g. "Short Term Memory"
       });
     });
   });
   ```

#### B. Question Options & Interactive UI Rendering
Each question item is evaluated using a 5-point Likert frequency scale.
* **Option Values & Labels:**
  | Value (Integer) | Display Label | Description |
  | :--- | :--- | :--- |
  | **`0`** | **Never** | The symptom/situation never occurs. |
  | **`1`** | **Rarely** | The symptom/situation occurs rarely. |
  | **`2`** | **Sometimes** | The symptom/situation occurs occasionally. |
  | **`3`** | **Often** | The symptom/situation occurs frequently. |
  | **`4`** | **Always** | The symptom/situation occurs constantly. |

* **UI/UX Design Best Practices:**
  * Render questions in a clean list or wizard interface.
  * For each question, render the 5 options in a horizontal/responsive grid.
  * Hide standard radio inputs and wrap them in styled `<label>` cards.
  * Selected options should be highlighted with a vibrant accent border (e.g., `2px solid var(--primary)` / `rgba(212,20,58,0.05)` background) and subtle shadow.
  * Display the category/domain tag above each question (e.g. "SHORT TERM MEMORY") for context.

#### C. Validation, Progress Tracking & User Controls
* **State Management:** Keep track of the selections in a key-value state object:
  ```javascript
  const [responses, setResponses] = useState({}); // { q1: 4, q2: 2, ... }
  ```
* **Real-time Progress:** Calculate the percentage of completion:
  ```javascript
  const progressPercent = Math.round((Object.keys(responses).length / totalQuestionsCount) * 100);
  ```
* **Submission Button Guard:** Keep the submission action disabled until every single question has received an answer:
  ```javascript
  const isFormComplete = Object.keys(responses).length === flatQuestions.length;
  ```

---

#### Step 7: Analyze Assessment Responses (AI Model Service)
Submits the compiled user answers to the model to run cognitive wellness scoring logic.
*   **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/analyze` (Proxied to `https://limitless-model.160-153-179-249.sslip.io`)
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    *   `assessmentId`: The identifier returned in Step 6.
    *   `age`: User's age.
    *   `gender`: Normalized gender string.
    *   `responses`: An array of items matching the following shape:
    ```json
    {
      "assessmentId": "assess_99a8b...",
      "age": 28,
      "gender": "male",
      "responses": [
        { "itemId": "q1", "value": 4 },
        { "itemId": "q2", "value": 2 }
      ]
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "overallScore": 82,
      "cognitiveAge": 26,
      "domains": {
        "memory": 85,
        "focus": 79
      },
      "recommendations": [
        "Read 15 minutes a day",
        "Perform cardiovascular exercise"
      ]
    }
    ```
    *Developer Action: Temporarily cache this response in `sessionStorage.setItem('analysisReport', JSON.stringify(report_json))`.*

#### Step 8: Save Assessment Results (Authenticated / Database Persistence)
> [!IMPORTANT]
> The AI model service is stateless and **does not save assessments**. The frontend MUST call this endpoint to persist the assessment in the DB so that history, dashboard trends, and reports remain available.
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/assessments`
*   **Request Headers:**
    *   `Content-Type: application/json`
    *   `Authorization: Bearer <authToken>`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "user_id": "6a4f5b...",
      "report_json": {
        "overallScore": 82,
        "cognitiveAge": 26,
        "domains": { "memory": 85, "focus": 79 },
        "recommendations": ["..."]
      },
      "pdf_url": null
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `201`):** Returns the complete created assessment object with the record `id`.

#### Step 9: Generate, Store, and Email Report PDF (Authenticated)
Generates the PDF report on the server, uploads it, updates the assessment record, and emails the PDF link directly to the user.
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/reports/:userId/pdf`
*   **Request Headers:**
    *   `Content-Type: application/json`
    *   `Authorization: Bearer <authToken>`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "analysis": {
        "overallScore": 82,
        "cognitiveAge": 26,
        "domains": { "memory": 85, "focus": 79 },
        "recommendations": ["..."]
      },
      "teaser": false, // Set to true if generating a locked/teaser PDF
      "sendEmail": true // Emails the link automatically to the registered address
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `201`):**
    ```json
    {
      "pdfUrl": "https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/files/pdf-reports/6a4f5b.../report_12345.pdf",
      "fileName": "report_12345.pdf",
      "assessment": {
        "id": "assess_db_id...",
        "user_id": "6a4f5b...",
        "pdf_url": "https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/files/pdf-reports/6a4f5b.../report_12345.pdf"
      }
    }
    ```
    *Note: The generated PDF can be downloaded directly from the returned `pdfUrl`.*

#### Step 10: View History / Dashboard (Authenticated)
Fetches the user details along with all completed assessments ordered by newest first.
*   **Endpoint:** `GET https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/users/:userId`
*   **Request Headers:**
    *   `Authorization: Bearer <authToken>`
*   **Response (Success `200`):**
    ```json
    {
      "id": "6a4f5b...",
      "name": "John Doe",
      "email": "user@example.com",
      "payment_status": "demo",
      "age": 28,
      "gender": "male",
      "assessments": [
        {
          "id": "assess_db_id...",
          "report_json": { ... },
          "pdf_url": "https://limitless-api...",
          "created_at": "2026-07-27T10:20:00Z"
        }
      ]
    }
    ```

#### Step 11: Contact Form / Enquiry Submissions (Public)
*   **Endpoint:** `POST https://limitless-api.160-153-179-249.sslip.io/api/enquiries`
*   **Request Headers:** `Content-Type: application/json`
*   **Request Body:**
    ```json
    {
      "name": "Query Sender",
      "email": "sender@example.com",
      "message": "Hello, I wanted to inquire about enterprise options."
    }
    ```
*   **Response (Success `201`):**
    ```json
    {
      "id": "enq_1298...",
      "name": "Query Sender",
      "email": "sender@example.com",
      "message": "Hello...",
      "status": "new",
      "created_at": "2026-07-27T10:22:00Z"
    }
    ```

